{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473422-possession-dominate-5-and-ghouls","id":1473422,"title":"Possession ( Dominate 5 ) and ghouls","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-27T13:16:54-08:00","id":1473422,"title":"Possession ( Dominate 5 ) and ghouls","content":"An elder vampire ( 7th generation ) spent several decades training his favorite ghoul.<br /> <br /> The elder's Disciplines:<br /> <br /> Celerity 3<br /> Fortitude 6<br /> Protean 4<br /> Dominate 5<br /> Auspex 3<br /> Thaumaturgy - several Paths and Rituals<br /> <br /> The ghouls Disciplines:<br /> <br /> Potence 2<br /> Fortitude 2<br /> Protean 1<br /> Dominate 1<br /> Obfuscation 1<br /> <br /> <br /> So, the question is: while using Possession on his Ghoul, can the Vampire use Disciplines? And if yes, what Disciplines and at what level?<br /> More specific questions:<br /> <br /> 1) The ghoul developed Potence ( istinctively, as all Ghouls ), the vampire don't know it. Can the vampire use it?<br /> 2) The ghoul developed Obfuscation while &quot;loaned&quot; to a Nosferatu ally. The vampire don't know it, can he use it?<br /> 3) The vampire know a physical discipline, Celerity, that the ghoul doesn't know. Can he use it?<br /> 4) The vampire know a mental discipline, Auspex, that the ghoul doesn't know. Can he use it<br /> 5) The vampire and the ghoul possess common physical ( Fortitude ) and mental ( Dominate ) disciplines. Can the vampire use them, and at what level?<br /> 6) Can the vampire use Thaumaturgy while possessing his ghoul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27051-solomon-draak","name":"Solomon Draak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27051_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-27T18:17:31-08:00","id":1473436,"title":"","content":"In my mind, Pot, Fort, and Cel are different from other disciplines, in that they become intertwinned with the flesh of the learner rather than the mind. Consequently a possessor can use them.if the body he possesses has them, even if he does not. Conversely, he can not bring them along if he possses someone who doesn't have them. Indeed, his body still has them while he's gone, even if Fort is the only one that still matters.<br /> <br /> Everything else is a mind power, and travels with the vampire's mind into the new body.So he can obfuscate and dominate and so forth normally, so long as the body he's in can pay the blood cost, assuming the discipline in question has a blood cost.<br /> <br /> That's my headcanon, anyway.<br /> <br /> The only one I'm not sure about is Protean. It's in a fuzzy area.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T12:42:00-08:00","id":1473492,"title":"","content":"The vampire should only be able to use the physical powers of the person he is possessing, but not any mental powers solely possessed by the person. <br /> <br /> He is no longer in his body so he clearly can't use powers associated with that form (and that includes mental powers and such since they still depend on him being a vampire). Possessing the other body &quot;locks&quot; the vampire out of his own. He may have the information to utilize such powers, but being in another body, it's useless information to him.<br /> <br /> He also clearly should not have any access to mental powers that are in the mind of the person, as he is merely hijacking the body.<br /> <br /> So what about &quot;mental&quot; powers that belong to both characters? Well, in my own chronicles this isn't an issue because I don't have ghouls know actual &quot;Disciplines&quot;, they just have access to some improved physical stats (as a result of vitae interacting with living body) that are simulated by the game as a Discipline. So that is not an issue I have to deal with. But in your scenario, I would say since the possessor understands and knows how to utilize such powers like Obfuscate 1, he can do so as the possessed ghoul.<br /> <br /> That's how I run them, or would run them, in my own chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T09:53:10-08:00","id":1473677,"title":"","content":"It's quite clearly written in the V20 rules on p155:<br /> <br /> 1. Vampires possessing ghouls can use the physical Disciplines the ghoul possesses, but not the mental ones<br /> <br /> 2. The vampire rolls Manipulation + Intimidation (difficulty 7) to determine how fully he assumes control of the mortal shell. Similar to the Animalism power Subsume the Spirit, multiple successes<br /> allow the character to utilize some mental Disciplines, noted on the chart below.<br /> <br /> Successes Result<br /> 1 success Cannot use Disciplines<br /> 2 successes Can use Auspex and other sensory powers<br /> 3 successes Can also use Presence and other powers of emotional manipulation<br /> 4 successes Can also use Dementation, Dominate, and other powers of mental manipulation<br /> 5 successes Can also use Chimerstry, Necromancy, Thaumaturgy, and other mystical powers<br /> <br /> It's pretty black and white, so to answer the original questions<br /> <br /> 1 - Yes because it's a physical Discipline the Ghoul has<br /> 2 - No because the vamp doesn't know it<br /> 3 - No because only mental Disciplines of the vamp can be used<br /> 4 - Yes, provided the vamp rolls sufficient successes<br /> 5 - Yes at the ghoul's level - see rule 1<br /> 6 - Same as answer 4","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}